{
    "summary": "Adds admin-initiated refunds, a signed payment-provider webhook, order status tracking, a customer order lookup and an HTML confirmation mail module, replacing notify.ts.",
    "findings": [
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:21",
            "finding": "`requireAdmin` also lets callers with `role === undefined` through, contradicting its own comment that anonymous callers are rejected. Anyone without a role can call `adminRefund`. The check should be `user.role !== \"admin\"`."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:46",
            "finding": "Signature verification runs only when `signature !== undefined`, so a request with no signature skips authentication. Anyone can mark orders paid or failed. A missing signature must be rejected."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:12",
            "finding": "`SECRET` defaults to an empty string when `PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset. The HMAC key is then publicly known and signatures are forgeable. Fail fast at startup instead."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/mail.ts:18",
            "finding": "The user-typed discount `code` is interpolated into the HTML mail without `escapeHtml`, although the other fields are escaped. This allows HTML injection in confirmation mails."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/api.ts:33",
            "finding": "`handleGetOrder` ignores `query.customerId` and returns any order by id. Any signed-in customer can read other customers' orders (IDOR). It needs to check `order.customer.id === query.customerId`."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/refund.ts:26",
            "finding": "`refundOrder` now refunds `order.subtotal` (the amount before the discount) instead of `order.total`. For discounted orders this refunds more than the customer paid."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "COVERAGE",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:40",
            "finding": "`adminRefund` does not validate `req.amount`. It accepts zero, negative or NaN values and amounts above `order.total`. It also does not check `refundsOf` for earlier refunds, so one order can be refunded repeatedly. The order status is not updated either."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:53-59",
            "finding": "`handlePaymentEvent` applies `markPaid`/`markFailed` regardless of the current status. A replayed or late event can flip a `cancelled` order (whose stock was already released) to `paid`, or a `paid` order to `failed`. Transitions should be guarded and made idempotent."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:15-22",
            "finding": "The hand-rolled `signaturesMatch` compares strings with `charCodeAt`. `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on buffers is the standard, less error-prone choice."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/api.ts:55",
            "finding": "The randomised `recommendations` helper is unrelated to refunds, webhooks or order status and is unused anywhere. It is scope creep and should be dropped or moved to its own change."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "PROPAGATION",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/store.ts:15",
            "finding": "`ordersOf` and `refundsOf` have no callers, and `OrderQuery.customerId` is never read. This is dead code left in the change."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CLARITY",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/mail.ts:35",
            "finding": "The `try/catch` wraps only an in-memory `outbox.push`, which cannot realistically throw. The retry-job rationale in the comment does not match the code, and `console.error` is left as diagnostic output."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "TESTING",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:45",
            "finding": "The change adds security-critical logic (signature check, amount parsing, role check, refund rules, status transitions) and the repository has no tests for any of it."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "DOCUMENTATION",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "README.md:3",
            "finding": "The README feature list does not mention the new admin refunds, payment webhook, order status or the required `PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET` setting."
        }
    ]
}
```

